  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: verified 0-sorry/0-axiom composite-modulus non-coprime Euler periodicity via CRT (PR #35013); answers euler-totient-oq-08 open question #1.",
    "builtItems": [
      "modEq_prod_of_pairwiseCoprime — reusable CRT assembly over a pairwise-coprime Finset (Proofs/EulerTotientOQ08OQ01.lean:57)",
      "pow_add_totient_modEq — headline a^(k+φ(n)) ≡ a^k [MOD n] (Proofs/EulerTotientOQ08OQ01.lean:84)",
      "pow_add_mul_totient_modEq, pow_modEq, pow_add_totient_modEq_of_le (Proofs/EulerTotientOQ08OQ01.lean:119,138,158)"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Composite case reduces to the parent prime-power result via CRT: n = ∏ p^{v_p(n)}, and φ(p^{v_p(n)}) ∣ φ(n) (Nat.totient_dvd_of_dvd on Nat.ordProj_dvd) makes the φ(n)-shift a whole number of periods on each factor.",
      "The sharp pre-period is k ≥ max_p v_p(n), phrased cleanly as ∀ p, n.factorization p ≤ k (non-primes give 0 ≤ k automatically).",
      "Factorisation-free sufficient condition n ≤ 2^k works because v_p(n) ≤ log_2 n; via Nat.factorization_le_of_le_pow with 2^k ≤ p^k."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Carmichael refinement: replace φ(n) with λ(n) = lcm_p λ(p^{v_p}) for the minimal period.",
      "Base-dependent pre-period max_p ceil(v_p(n)/max(1,v_p(a))) sharper than max_p v_p(n).",
      "Eventual periodicity for tetration towers a↑↑m mod n."
    ],
